### IntelliJ / VS Code REST Client requests. Run them top to bottom.

### Place a high-value order (waits for approval)
POST http://localhost:8080/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": "42",
  "customerId": "cust-7",
  "lines": [{ "sku": "SKU-1", "quantity": 3 }],
  "total": 7500,
  "shippingAddress": "1 Rue X, Casablanca"
}

### Same order again -> 409 Conflict (workflow id = order id)
POST http://localhost:8080/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": "42",
  "customerId": "cust-7",
  "lines": [{ "sku": "SKU-1", "quantity": 3 }],
  "total": 7500,
  "shippingAddress": "1 Rue X, Casablanca"
}

### Query its status -> AWAITING_APPROVAL
GET http://localhost:8080/orders/42

### Approve (signal)
POST http://localhost:8080/orders/42/approve?by=alice

### Status -> COMPLETED with a tracking number
GET http://localhost:8080/orders/42

### Cancel (signal) - try it on a new order before approving
POST http://localhost:8080/orders/42/cancel?reason=changed+my+mind
